# **Never rewrite a byte of this repository.**
#
# `corpus_content_hash` in governed-bi digests every file in the corpus subtrees, byte for byte,
# and that digest is the treatment identity a measured number is pinned to. Git's end-of-line
# conversion is on by default on Windows (`core.autocrlf=true`), so without this line the assets
# are stored LF and checked out CRLF — and a fresh clone would compute a *different* corpus hash
# from the tree that produced the number, on the same commit. Reproducibility from a clean
# checkout is the entire reason this repo exists, so the conversion has to be off, declared here
# rather than left to whatever each contributor has configured.
* -text
